Parity reproduced from the web source (THE spec):
  - data: useVehicles + useBatteryDegradation(DegradationData) bound via the state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view)
  - chartData -> points(): month/health(avg_health)/range(avg_range)/original(trend[0].avg_range)
  - currentHealth = current_health_pct ?? current_health ?? nil ; degradationRate = degradation_rate_pct_per_month ; cycles = current_cycles
  - stats memo: SoH (always, "—" if nil), Degradation (only when rate>0, "−x.xx%" + "/mo", U+2212 minus), Cycles (always, "—" if nil)
  - chart: chartData.length>1 -> area(health) with YAxis [dataMin-2 .. 100] + ReferenceLine y=80 ; else "More data needed for trend"
  - isCompact = cols<=1 && rows<=1 ; isEmpty = currentHealth==nil && chartData.length==0
  - WidgetShell title "Battery Degradation" + down-trend icon ; empty "No degradation data"
  States rendered: loading / empty / error / stale (chip + 30s auto-refresh) / offline (cached + chip) / content / needs-more-data.
  i18n: every web key resolved through the facade — widget.soh, widget.degradation, widget.mo, widget.cycles, widget.healthPct,
        widget.needMoreData, widget.batteryDegradation, widget.noDegradation (+ namespaced native chrome keys). No English literals in code.
  a11y: VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (refresh/open/retry), chart trend + per-point values, combined stat cells; Dynamic Type
        via Font.TS tokens; Reduce-Motion respected (chart animation gated).
  Telemetry: model.start() emits the P1/S11 view.opened event with surface slug "BatteryDegradationTrendWidget" (idempotent — asserted).

